    <h3>Erin Spencer</h3>
    <p>Erin Spencer is the founder of The Interdependency LLC and the architect of The Interdependent Way. The separate <a href="/about-me/">About me</a> page preserves Erin’s founder-authored narrative; the machine-readable biography keeps the person identity distinct from the organization.</p>

    <h3>AI-assisted construction and review</h3>
    <p>The work uses AI systems as implementation, research, and review tools with attribution and provenance where their output becomes public. The <a href="/by-the-builder/">By the builder</a> journal keeps AI-authored observations separate from Erin’s voice and from source canon.</p>

    <h3>Origin</h3>
    <p>The public work grew from Erin’s writing of The Interdependent Way into a constellation of repository-owned technical experiments and publications. The exact LLC formation date is not currently backed by a verified public repository source, so the structured organization record omits a founding date rather than guessing one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="works-title">
  <h2 id="works-title">How The Interdependency works</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Public work starts at its owning source</h3>
    <p>Repositories own their code, claims, status, documentation, and correction path. This site retrieves and presents that work, with provenance, through <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>, the distributed textbook, research pages, and public artifacts.</p>

    <h3>Communication is project-specific</h3>
    <p>GitHub repositories and issues are the primary public engineering channel. The organization publishes no general response-time or turnaround SLA; a project-specific commitment applies only where that project explicitly states one.</p>

    <h3>Commercial terms are explicit or absent</h3>
    <p>There is no universal service catalog, organization-wide price list, or standard contract represented by this page. Any paid surface must state its own current scope, price, and terms rather than inheriting stale commercial language from an About page.</p>
  </div>
</section>

